Vendored JSON Schemas for wpbr-license/v1, used by the self-test stub.

Source repository: WPBrewer/wpbr-license-server (private)
Source commit: da084ce
Source path: contract/schema/
Copied from the public snapshot in WPBrewer/wpbr-updater tests/contract/schema
(that snapshot's SOURCE file: "Snapshot taken 2026-11-11 from the archive attached to WPB-369").

The schemas are what the stub implements. $id and $ref use
https://wpbrewer.com/schema/wpbr-license/v1/.

POST /releases behavior follows the da084ce api-v1.md text: HTTP Basic
application password, multipart parts metadata (application/json) and zip,
HTTP 200 with status draft, HTTP 409 invalid_request when the version was
used before (including after a yank or a delete, and including an identical
sha256). Publishing is not a REST route. The stub's
POST /releases/{id}/publish route is a test-only stand-in.

POST /releases/{id}/yank and the update-info offer rules (yanked rows are
never packaged; the previous published release is offered with
allow_downgrade when it is older; pinned_version caps the offer; an invalid
pin offers nothing; expired is 403 license_expired; revoked is 200 with no
package) follow that same api-v1.md text. They are not separate schema files
in the da084ce snapshot. The stub's logged-in-session auth is not implemented;
the workflow sends the application password. A user without
manage_wpbr_releases is the fixture wpbr-nocap.
